## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to influence across teams, design a low-risk pilot, and formalize a deprecation plan with measurable success metrics.

## Key Concepts

- Stakeholder mapping and influence without authority
- Pilot design with feature flags and parallel paths
- Data-driven success criteria and deprecation thresholds
- Risk management, comms, and documentation

## Code Example

```javascript
if (featureFlags.gatewayMigrateEnabled) {
  routeToNewGateway(req);
} else {
  routeToLegacyGateway(req);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you respond if adoption stalls despite favorable metrics?
- What would you include in the risk register to escalate if critical incidents arise during the pilot?

## Why This Is Asked
This assesses ownership, bias for action, and customer obsession during a real outage versus delivery trade-off.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end ownership during incidents
- Rapid containment and safe rollout strategies
- Clear customer/executive communication and transparency
- Post-mortem with measurable metrics and preventative actions

## Code Example
```javascript
// Runbook sketch for incident containment
function runIncidentRunbook() {
  declareIncident();
  triageTeam();
  implementContainment();
  assessImpact();
  communicateStatus();
  rollbackOrPatch();
  postMortem();
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to handle production data quality issues during migration, enforce governance, and execute a safe rollback or delta-based fix under constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-database migration and cutover planning
- Data quality remediation and reconciliation
- Rollback strategy and risk assessment
- Governance, audit logging, and data masking

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation: reconcile deltas and validate integrity
async function reconcileAndValidate(src, dest, checkpoint) {
  const delta = await computeDelta(src, dest, checkpoint);
  if (delta.discrepancies.length > 0) {
    await applyCorrections(dest, delta);
    await validateIntegrity(dest, checkpoint);
  }
  return { status: 'validated', delta };
}
```

